  "limits": [
    "Partial Commander registrations and controlled boards are not complete legal decks or pregame fixtures.",
    "Thirteen native cases include ten paid card paths, one paid Vesuvan cast followed by a controlled native face-down event, and two synthetic memory contracts.",
    "Eleven packaged witnesses cover the paid paths and controlled event. The blink outcome is an existing positive control.",
    "Phase advancement uses real bounded hooks without response priority. Postcombat initial states avoid incidental AI combat changing the tested boards.",
    "The face-down event tests the cleanup condition, not optional upkeep choice, admission or special-action timing.",
    "Synthetic imprinted/remembered setup does not claim a printed Grizzly Bears imprint ability. Card-owner filtering uses copied-world membership; remembered players remain retained under the existing native contract.",
    "Only Card and Player remembered values are restored; the native restoration already omitted other kinds. This is not a general arbitrary-payload restoration mechanism.",
    "Two same-deadline overlapping frames and one blink guard do not certify all overlapping memory lifetimes, clone-source/target transitions, copy exceptions or room layouts.",
    "Eiganjo checks end-of-turn keyword cleanup and intrinsic vigilance, not every token, pump duration or AI policy.",
    "Other callbacks, merged/perpetual state, hidden views, arbitrary continuations and unexamined fields remain open. Normal CLI reports still do not aggregate the native unmapped-command diagnostic.",
    "Selected versioned rules and retained catalog records do not certify every current rule or card."
  ]
